---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
// Draft written from what the site actually does (Oct 2026). Review before launch, and update if analytics,
// pixels or Slack notifications for leads are added.
const updated = '30 October 2026';
---
<Base title="Privacy and cookies" description="What personal data wavimedia.com collects, why, and your rights.">
  <Hero crumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy & cookies' }]} eyebrow="Legal" pad="96px">
    <h1 class="h1">Privacy &amp; cookies</h1>
    <p class="lead" style="margin-top:32px">Plain truth applies here too. This page explains what this website collects, why, and what you can ask us to do with it.</p>
  </Hero>
  <section class="s-paper section">
    <article class="container legal">
      <p class="label">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>Wavi Media is responsible for the personal data collected through wavimedia.com. Questions about privacy, or requests about your data, go to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>

      <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
      <h3>When you contact us</h3>
      <p>When you send the form on our contact page, we receive the details you enter: your name, work email, website, phone number, where your business is based, and, if you choose to share them, your revenue range, what you need help with and your message.</p>
      <p>We use them only to reply to you and to prepare a possible collaboration. The legal basis is taking steps at your request before entering into an agreement, and our legitimate interest in answering enquiries (GDPR Article 6(1)(b) and (f)). We don’t add you to a newsletter or share your details with anyone for their own marketing.</p>
      <p>We keep enquiries for as long as they are relevant to our dialogue with you. If no collaboration comes of it, we delete them when they are no longer needed. You can ask us to delete them at any time.</p>

      <h3>When you use our free tools</h3>
      <p>The profit check and growth score run entirely in your browser. Nothing you enter is sent to us or stored.</p>
      <p>The store scan sends the store address you enter to our server, which reads that store’s public homepage and returns the report. We don’t store the report. Our hosting logs record which address was scanned, for a short period, to keep the service running and to stop misuse.</p>

      <h3>When you visit the site</h3>
      <p>Like any website, our hosting provider processes technical data such as your IP address, browser type and the pages requested, in order to deliver the site and keep it secure. This is based on our legitimate interest in running a working, secure website. Our fonts are hosted on our own site, so visiting does not send your data to a font service.</p>

      <h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
      <p>This site uses no tracking or advertising cookies, and no analytics that identify you. That is why you don’t see a cookie banner. If that changes, we will ask for your consent first and update this page.</p>

      <h2>Who processes data for us</h2>
      <p>We use a small number of providers who process data on our behalf and only on our instructions:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Vercel</strong> hosts the website and runs the contact form and store scan.</li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong> delivers the contact form to our inbox by email.</li>
        <li>Our email provider stores the enquiries we receive.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Some of these providers are based in or process data in the United States. Where data leaves the EU/EEA, it is protected by the safeguards the GDPR requires, such as the EU Commission’s standard contractual clauses or the EU-US Data Privacy Framework.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You have the right to access the personal data we hold about you, to have it corrected or deleted, to restrict or object to how we use it, and to receive it in a portable format. Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will answer within one month.</p>
      <p>You can also complain to a data protection authority, in particular where you live or work. In Denmark that is Datatilsynet (datatilsynet.dk).</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If we change how we handle personal data, we update this page and the date at the top.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .legal { max-width: 820px; }
  .legal h2 { margin: 64px 0 0; font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 500; font-size: clamp(30px, 3vw, 40px); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
  .legal h3 { margin: 36px 0 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; }
  .legal p, .legal li { font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--slate); }
  .legal p { margin: 14px 0 0; }
  .legal ul { margin: 14px 0 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  .legal li + li { margin-top: 8px; }
  .legal strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .legal a { color: var(--ink); }
</style>
